# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Setup Notes

This file explains how to run and inspect the generated scaffold without rereading the Bankstack source repository.

## Install

Use pnpm only:

```bash
pnpm install
```

The generated `packageManager` and engine fields pin the expected pnpm and Node versions.

## Verify Locally

These commands should work before you create any Cloudflare or Supabase account:

```bash
pnpm check
pnpm build
pnpm test
pnpm verify
```

`pnpm dev` starts the three app surfaces through Nx. If you prefer separate terminals, use:

```bash
pnpm --filter @{{PROJECT_NAME}}/api dev
pnpm --filter @{{PROJECT_NAME}}/dashboard dev
pnpm --filter @{{PROJECT_NAME}}/marketing dev
```

## Layout

- `apps/marketing`: public Astro surface.
- `apps/dashboard`: SvelteKit dashboard, Cloudflare-ready with `adapter-cloudflare`.
- `apps/api`: Hono API, runnable locally with Node and shaped for Workers.
- `packages/ui`: shared Tailwind v4 theme CSS and tiny primitives.
- `packages/supabase`: shared Supabase env contracts and auth/RLS boundary notes.
- `packages/shared-utils`: cross-app constants and Zod helpers.
- `supabase/`: placeholder for future migrations after a real project exists.

## Cloudflare Boundary

`apps/dashboard/wrangler.jsonc` and `apps/api/wrangler.jsonc` are safe examples. They follow the current Cloudflare Wrangler JSONC shape and show the intended dashboard-to-API service binding:

```jsonc
"services": [
  {
    "binding": "API",
    "service": "{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api"
  }
]
```

Cloudflare resources are not provisioned by the CLI. When you are ready to deploy, install dependencies, authenticate with Wrangler, replace names as needed, generate Worker types, and deploy intentionally.

References:

- https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/configuration/
- https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/service-bindings/
- https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/adapter-cloudflare

## Supabase Boundary

Supabase credentials are optional for local scaffold verification and required for real auth/data. Start from the `.env.example` files and replace placeholder values only after you create a Supabase project.

Use browser-visible `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*` values only for public URL and publishable key configuration. Keep JWT verification and any secret values on the server. For protected data, verify the user server-side and rely on row level security policies for exposed tables.

References:

- https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys
- https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/server-side
- https://supabase.com/docs/reference/javascript/auth-getuser

## v0.1 Limits

Bankstack v0.1 is scaffolding plus conventions. It intentionally does not include Python compute, product tables, background workers, deployment automation, or a complete Supabase Auth UI.

## Provider AI Tooling

Optional provider AI tooling guidance, when selected, is written to [AI_TOOLS.md](AI_TOOLS.md). It is safe documentation only: no provider installer commands are run, no MCP credentials are written, and no Cloudflare or Supabase resources are provisioned.
